  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Sushil is a diabetic patient. He is only allowed to eat **at most** KKK calories in a day. However, he likes to eat sweets a lot.\n\nThere are NNN sweets in front of him. The iii-th sweet has a calorie count of AiA_iAi​.\n\nSushil will eat the sweets **in order**, i.e. he will start from the 111-st sweet, then the 222-nd, then the 333-rd, and so on.\n\nIf eating the iii-th sweet would take him over his daily calorie limit, he will not eat it, and he will also **not eat any further sweets.**\n\nFind the maximum number of sweets Sushil can eat without exceeding his calorie limit.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the number of sweets and the calorie limit, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers — A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum number of sweets Sushil can eat in order without exceeding his calorie limit.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100",
      "1≤K≤1041 \\le K \\le 10^41≤K≤104"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 10\n5 2 5 2\n4 5\n2 1 1 1\n3 10\n11 1 1",
        "output": "2\n4\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Sushil can eat the first 222 sweets for a total calorie count of 5+2=75+2=75+2=7. If he tries to eat the 333rd sweet, he exceeds his calorie limit of 101010, so he immediately stops.\nTest case 333: Sushil is unable to eat the first sweet itself because it has 111111 calories and he can have at most 101010 calories."
      }
    ]
  },
